IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc1-s7-space.l4 -- section 7, subsections (2.3) to (2.38): the Space Station and the Lunar Gateway.
-- Acts or omissions outside Canada by Canadian crew members and by crew members of Partner States, the consent of the Attorney General of Canada,
-- and the definitions that apply in those subsections.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The definitions are functions over facts. A definition that says it has the same meaning as in another Act is a pass-through of the answer of that Act
-- (a borrowed term is asked as an input, as the Commons guide says). The answers of the definitions are passed to the offence rules as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs.
-- A period ("space flight") is tested on a number the person states: the moments are in hours on one clock, in the same unit; both end-points are inside the period
-- ("begins with the launching ... ends with their landing").

§ `Section 7(2.34) -- Definitions for subsections (2.3) and (2.31)`

-- src:377 | Definitions
-- src:378 | (2.34) The definitions in this subsection apply in this subsection and in subsections (2.3) and (2.31).
-- src:379 | Agreement has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Civil International Space Station Agreement Implementation Act. (Accord)
@ref s 7(2.34) Agreement (src:377-379)
GIVEN `it has the meaning Agreement has in section 2 of the Civil International Space Station Agreement Implementation Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) Agreement` MEANS `it has the meaning Agreement has in section 2 of the Civil International Space Station Agreement Implementation Act`   -- the text hands the definition to that Act: its answer is carried through unchanged, NOTHING included

-- src:383 | crew member of a Partner State means a crew member of the Space Station who is
-- src:384 | (a) a citizen of a Partner State; or
-- src:385 | (b) a citizen of a state, other than Canada or a Partner State, who is authorized by a Partner State to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element. (membre d’équipage d’un État partenaire)
@ref s 7(2.34) crew member of a Partner State (src:383-385)
GIVEN `it is a crew member of the Space Station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a citizen of a Partner State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a citizen of a state other than Canada or a Partner State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized by a Partner State to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) crew member of a Partner State` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a crew member of the Space Station` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crew member of a Partner State means a crew member of the Space Station who is"
        IF `the person is a citizen of a Partner State` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a citizen of a state other than Canada or a Partner State` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `authorized by a Partner State` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a citizen of a Partner State` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the state is a Partner State was not answered
        IF (`the person is a citizen of a state other than Canada or a Partner State` EQUALS NOTHING) AND `authorized by a Partner State` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the state is a Partner State was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crew member of a Partner State means a crew member of the Space Station who is"
    WHERE
        `authorized by a Partner State` MEANS `the person is authorized by a Partner State to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element`

-- src:380 | Canadian crew member means a crew member of the Space Station who is
-- src:381 | (a) a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:382 | (b) a citizen of a foreign state, other than a Partner State, who is authorized by Canada to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element. (membre d’équipage canadien)
@ref s 7(2.34) Canadian crew member (src:380-382)
GIVEN `it is a crew member of the Space Station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a citizen of a foreign state other than a Partner State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized by Canada to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) Canadian crew member` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a crew member of the Space Station` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Canadian crew member means a crew member of the Space Station who is"
        IF `the person is a Canadian citizen` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a citizen of a foreign state other than a Partner State` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is authorized by Canada to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a citizen of a foreign state other than a Partner State` EQUALS NOTHING) AND `the person is authorized by Canada to act as a crew member for a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the state is a Partner State was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Canadian crew member means a crew member of the Space Station who is"

-- src:386 | flight element means a Space Station element provided by Canada or by a Partner State under the Agreement and under any memorandum of understanding or other implementing arrangement entered into to carry out the Agreement. (élément de vol)
@ref s 7(2.34) flight element (src:386-386)
GIVEN `it is a Space Station element` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided by Canada or by a Partner State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided under the Agreement and under any memorandum of understanding or other implementing arrangement entered into to carry out the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) flight element` MEANS
    IF `it is a Space Station element` AND `it is provided by Canada or by a Partner State` AND `it is provided under the Agreement and under any memorandum of understanding or other implementing arrangement entered into to carry out the Agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "flight element means a Space Station element provided by Canada or by a Partner State"

-- src:387 | Partner State means a State, other than Canada, who contracted to enter into the Agreement and for which the Agreement has entered into force in accordance with article 25 of the Agreement. (État partenaire)
@ref s 7(2.34) Partner State (src:387-387)
GIVEN `it is a State other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contracted to enter into the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Agreement has entered into force for it in accordance with article 25 of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) Partner State` MEANS
    IF `it is a State other than Canada` AND `it contracted to enter into the Agreement` AND `the Agreement has entered into force for it in accordance with article 25 of the Agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Partner State means a State, other than Canada"

-- src:388 | space flight means the period that begins with the launching of a crew member of the Space Station, continues during their stay in orbit and ends with their landing on earth. (vol spatial)
@ref s 7(2.34) space flight (src:388-388)
GIVEN `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment of the launching of a crew member of the Space Station` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment of their landing on earth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) the moment is within the space flight` MEANS
    IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` AT LEAST `the moment of the launching of a crew member of the Space Station`
       AND `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` AT MOST `the moment of their landing on earth`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "space flight means the period that begins with the launching of a crew member of the Space Station, continues during their stay in orbit and ends with their landing on earth"

-- src:389 | Space Station means the civil international Space Station that is a multi-use facility in low-earth orbit, with flight elements and dedicated ground elements provided by, or on behalf of, Canada or the Partner States. (station spatiale)
@ref s 7(2.34) Space Station (src:389-389)
GIVEN `it is the civil international Space Station that is a multi-use facility in low-earth orbit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has flight elements and dedicated ground elements provided by, or on behalf of, Canada or the Partner States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.34) Space Station` MEANS
    IF `it is the civil international Space Station that is a multi-use facility in low-earth orbit` AND `it has flight elements and dedicated ground elements provided by, or on behalf of, Canada or the Partner States`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Space Station means the civil international Space Station"

§ `Section 7(2.3) and (2.31) -- Space Station: Canadian crew members and crew members of Partner States`

-- src:366 | Space Station — Canadian crew members
-- src:367 | (2.3) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, a Canadian crew member who, during a space flight, commits an act or omission outside Canada that if committed in Canada would constitute an indictable offence is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada, if that act or omission is committed
-- src:368 | (a) on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station; or
-- src:369 | (b) on any means of transportation to or from the Space Station.
-- src:370 | Space Station — crew members of Partner States
-- src:371 | (2.31) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, a crew member of a Partner State who commits an act or omission outside Canada during a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station or on any means of transportation to and from the Space Station that if committed in Canada would constitute an indictable offence is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada, if that act or omission
-- src:372 | (a) threatens the life or security of a Canadian crew member; or
-- src:373 | (b) is committed on or in relation to, or damages, a flight element provided by Canada.
@ref s 7(2.3) (src:366-373)
DECLARE `s 7(2.3) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.3)(a) the act or omission is committed on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station`
    `s 7(2.3)(b) the act or omission is committed on any means of transportation to or from the Space Station`

@ref s 7(2.3) (src:366-369)
GIVEN `the person is a Canadian crew member, by s 7(2.34)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.3) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.3) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a Canadian crew member, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the act or omission is during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(2.34) did not answer whether the person is a Canadian crew member or the moment is within a space flight
        IF `the person is a Canadian crew member, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the act or omission is during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Canadian crew member who, during a space flight, commits an act or omission"
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would constitute an indictable offence"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada, if that act or omission is committed"

-- src:370 | Space Station — crew members of Partner States
-- src:371 | (2.31) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, a crew member of a Partner State who commits an act or omission outside Canada during a space flight on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station or on any means of transportation to and from the Space Station that if committed in Canada would constitute an indictable offence is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada, if that act or omission
-- src:372 | (a) threatens the life or security of a Canadian crew member; or
-- src:373 | (b) is committed on or in relation to, or damages, a flight element provided by Canada.
@ref s 7(2.31) (src:370-373)
DECLARE `s 7(2.31) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(2.31)(a) the act or omission threatens the life or security of a Canadian crew member`
    `s 7(2.31)(b) the act or omission is committed on or in relation to, or damages, a flight element provided by Canada`

