GIVEN `the person is a crew member of a Partner State, by s 7(2.34)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is outside Canada during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station or on any means of transportation to and from the Space Station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence`
      grounds IS A LIST OF `s 7(2.31) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.31) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a crew member of a Partner State, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the act or omission is outside Canada during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 7(2.34) did not answer whether the person is a crew member of a Partner State or the moment is within a space flight
        IF `the person is a crew member of a Partner State, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the act or omission is outside Canada during a space flight, by s 7(2.34)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a crew member of a Partner State who commits an act or omission outside Canada during a space flight"
        IF NOT `it is on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station or on any means of transportation to and from the Space Station` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on, or in relation to, a flight element of the Space Station or on any means of transportation to and from the Space Station"
        IF `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would constitute an indictable offence"
        IF NOT (null grounds) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada, if that act or omission"

-- (2.32) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 4]
-- src:374 | (2.32) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 4]
@ref s 7(2.32) (src:374-374)
`s 7(2.32) as the text shows it` MEANS "[Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 4]"

-- src:375 | Consent of Attorney General of Canada
-- src:376 | (2.33) No proceedings in relation to an offence referred to in subsection (2.3) or (2.31) may be instituted without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 7(2.33) (src:375-376)
GIVEN `the offence is one referred to in subsection (2.3) or (2.31)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the Attorney General of Canada has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2.33) the proceedings are barred for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is one referred to in subsection (2.3) or (2.31)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an offence referred to in subsection (2.3) or (2.31)"
        IF `the consent of the Attorney General of Canada has been obtained` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

